### Import normalization

- Remove supported runtime-only fields from imported data.
- Record their removal as a non-blocking note.
- Do not report harmless runtime-field removal as an error.
- Apply documented schema defaults safely.
- Preserve imported node IDs exactly. Never silently regenerate imported IDs.
- Keep legitimate user data.
- Do not silently discard arbitrary unknown fields unless the specified schema explicitly classifies them as removable runtime fields.

Normalization must be idempotent:

`normalize(normalize(document))` must deep-equal `normalize(document)`.

## 10. Stable deterministic export

For the same graph state, export must produce byte-identical JSON.

Enforce all of the following:

- Nodes remain in store order.
- Edges remain in store order.
- Do not sort nodes or edges.
- Object keys follow a fixed, documented schema order.
- Indentation is exactly two spaces.
- The exported text ends with exactly the intended trailing newline.
- Runtime/UI fields are excluded.
- The version is included.
- Serialization does not mutate the live graph.

A graph exported twice without changes must produce identical text.

Use the same deterministic serializer for the preview, Copy, and Download paths.

